# SPECIFICATION-DRIVEN DEVELOPMENT RULES

## Execution Tracks & Token Optimization

### Track 1: Fast Track (Bug fixes, UI/CSS hotfixes, minor isolated refactors)
- Scope: Triggered for bug fixes, CSS tweaks, mobile layout bugs, or single-file changes.
- Rules:
  1. DO NOT read constitution.md, ./ARCHITECTURE.md, or the specs/ directory.
  2. Directly inspect and modify only the targeted component/file mentioned in the prompt.
  3. Keep changes minimal and isolated.

### Track 2: Spec-Driven Track (New features, complex architectural changes)
- Scope: Triggered ONLY when explicit slash commands are used (/speckit.*) or when explicitly requested to build/plan a full feature.
- Rules:
  1. Read constitution.md (Core principles & invariant constraints).
  2. Read ./ARCHITECTURE.md (Detailed architectural guidelines).
  3. Inspect the active specification file in specs/.
  4. Never make unverified architectural changes or modify Prisma schemas without explicit instructions in the spec.

## Invariant Constraints (Applies to All Tracks)
- Public UI Policy: 100% English across all components (pages, modals, cards, badges, buttons, toasts, placeholders).
- Localization: Keep translations clean and synchronized in src/locales/en/.
- Quality Gate: Before marking any task complete, verify zero TypeScript errors via npx tsc --noEmit and ensure npm run build succeeds.
